WEBVTT

00:01.209 --> 00:04.421
[♪ opening theme song playing]

01:30.173 --> 01:31.341
LIGHT AND DARKNESS

01:31.383 --> 01:32.384
[buzzer rings]

01:32.676 --> 01:34.177
[LERONIRA] You may now
submit your ballots

01:34.219 --> 01:35.679
for our fourth vote.

01:36.555 --> 01:39.058
[NAO] We were just going through
the motions at that point.

01:39.600 --> 01:42.352
The fight was over
after the first round,

01:42.728 --> 01:44.605
and I had lost.

01:44.772 --> 01:47.315
But we still had to vote.

01:48.442 --> 01:50.986
[LERONIRA] Please stand by
while we tally the votes.

01:51.278 --> 01:53.781
FOURTH VOTE

01:54.364 --> 01:56.324
FIFTH VOTE

02:03.206 --> 02:04.583
[Hitomi laughs]

02:04.625 --> 02:06.752
Oh, man, I almost feel bad.

02:06.794 --> 02:07.836
You want me to ask

02:07.920 --> 02:09.713
if they'll put you
out of your misery?

02:09.755 --> 02:12.382
It's bad enough
without you rubbing it in.

02:12.424 --> 02:15.343
I wouldn't have to
if this game weren't so boring.

02:16.929 --> 02:18.179
- Say...
- [Nao gasps]

02:18.263 --> 02:21.642
How about we spice things up
with a side game?

02:21.683 --> 02:23.435
Come on, it'll be fun.

02:23.477 --> 02:25.562
And if you win,
I'll give you all 30 votes

02:25.604 --> 02:27.439
I've collected thus far.

02:27.481 --> 02:28.649
We can do that?

02:28.690 --> 02:30.776
Aren't votes set
after they're tallied?

02:30.818 --> 02:32.402
In another game, sure.

02:32.444 --> 02:34.029
But in this one,
the votes we get

02:34.071 --> 02:35.614
are just another resource.

02:35.656 --> 02:39.367
And buying resources
is what M Tickets are for.

02:39.409 --> 02:42.537
[STAFF] Yes, it's allowed.
So long as both parties agree,

02:42.579 --> 02:43.914
we can transfer the votes.

02:43.956 --> 02:45.499
But the change
won't appear on the board

02:45.540 --> 02:47.084
until after the next tally.

02:47.126 --> 02:48.961
- Told you.
- [Nao sighs]

02:49.377 --> 02:51.421
So then,
what do you get if I lose?

02:51.463 --> 02:55.676
One of your M Tickets made out
for 30 million yen, what else?

02:56.259 --> 02:59.262
[NAO] That's a lot of money.
But I have to get votes somehow.

02:59.304 --> 03:00.889
And since
no one will talk to me,

03:00.931 --> 03:02.724
this might be my only chance.

03:02.766 --> 03:04.601
[HITOMI] So, you in?

03:04.643 --> 03:06.854
What would we be playing, exactly?

03:06.895 --> 03:09.023
I was thinking something
quick and dirty.

03:09.064 --> 03:10.107
[NAO] Mm?

03:10.565 --> 03:12.026
Cards?

03:12.526 --> 03:15.403
I brought them along in case
I needed to kill some time.

03:15.445 --> 03:18.365
But you've never seen
a deck like this one before.

03:19.616 --> 03:21.618
[gasps] Is that a misprint?

03:21.660 --> 03:24.788
It happens sometimes
with these mass-produced ones.

03:24.830 --> 03:27.332
Lucky for us, a joker
and a double-backed card

03:27.374 --> 03:28.625
are all we need.

03:29.376 --> 03:30.878
Tell me something.

03:31.252 --> 03:34.756
If you had to pick, would you go
with light or darkness?

03:35.049 --> 03:38.677
Oh, well. If you mean
in general, then light.

03:38.719 --> 03:41.346
Ah... Now, back to the game.

03:41.388 --> 03:43.724
First, I'll drop our two cards
into this bag

03:43.765 --> 03:45.934
and give it a little shake
like so.

03:46.518 --> 03:49.146
Next, you'll reach in
and blind draw one of them.

03:49.188 --> 03:51.565
And then, depending
on which card you pulled,

03:51.606 --> 03:53.025
you or I will score a point.

03:53.067 --> 03:54.109
[NAO] Sounds easy.

03:54.275 --> 03:56.611
Now, there's
one big caveat to all of this.

03:56.653 --> 03:58.613
If you pull your card
and it's the Joker,

03:58.655 --> 04:00.448
it'll ruin the suspense.

04:00.490 --> 04:03.035
We need it face down
so it could be either.

04:03.077 --> 04:05.579
Then you put the card
on the table and flip it.

04:05.620 --> 04:06.955
If it's "light," you win.

04:06.997 --> 04:09.457
For our game,
the Joker will be the "light."

04:09.499 --> 04:10.709
Since I'm "dark,"

04:10.792 --> 04:13.252
I get a point every time
you pull the misprint.

04:13.294 --> 04:14.880
If you pull the card face up,

04:14.922 --> 04:17.049
you'll put it back
and try again.

04:18.133 --> 04:21.553
Then rinse and repeat
until one of us gets ten points.

04:21.595 --> 04:23.097
Simple, no?

04:23.597 --> 04:26.141
So simple, in fact,
that there's no way to cheat.

04:26.183 --> 04:27.935
I mix up the cards,
you draw them,

04:27.976 --> 04:29.394
and luck decides who wins.

04:29.436 --> 04:31.354
That's about as fair
as you can get.

04:31.396 --> 04:34.149
That's it. You down?

04:34.191 --> 04:35.609
[Nao breathes uneasily]

04:36.026 --> 04:37.694
Yeah, let's do it.

04:38.486 --> 04:40.864
[NAO] Thirty votes
for 30 million yen.

04:40.906 --> 04:43.324
There was a kind of odd balance
to it on paper.

04:43.366 --> 04:45.911
We put it on an M Ticket
to make it official.

04:45.953 --> 04:48.956
But it wasn't real
until we started playing.

04:51.208 --> 04:52.417
[Nao breathes nervously]

04:52.459 --> 04:54.795
Well, don't keep me in suspense.

04:57.131 --> 05:00.217
All right, it's the Joker.
That's one point for me.

05:00.259 --> 05:01.593
You sneak.

05:01.635 --> 05:04.221
Keep this up and you'll have
my votes in no time.

05:04.263 --> 05:06.098
NAO
FUKUNAGA

05:11.519 --> 05:12.520
[Nao gasps]

05:12.813 --> 05:15.398
[chuckles] Remember,
the odds are fifty-fifty,

05:15.440 --> 05:17.734
so it was bound to happen
eventually.

05:17.776 --> 05:19.278
NAO
FUKUNAGA

05:19.318 --> 05:21.238
[NAO] On and on we went.

05:21.280 --> 05:23.824
Card, after card, after card.

05:24.992 --> 05:27.410
Until it was all over.

05:27.452 --> 05:28.745
NAO
FUKUNAGA

05:28.787 --> 05:30.831
[Nao cries]

05:31.665 --> 05:34.333
[Hitomi laughs]

05:36.503 --> 05:39.089
Poor Nao.
Too honest to ever cheat,

05:39.131 --> 05:41.466
yet too unlucky to ever win.

05:43.510 --> 05:46.805
Oh, well, at least
we had fun, right?

05:46.847 --> 05:48.182
[NAO] I lost.

05:48.223 --> 05:50.892
I had a second chance
fall right into my lap,

05:50.934 --> 05:53.436
and I'd used it
to make things worse.

05:54.562 --> 05:55.981
[Nao continues crying]

06:00.319 --> 06:01.611
[door opens]

06:01.653 --> 06:04.239
[Akiyama sighs]
What is it this time?

06:04.281 --> 06:05.490
Who?

06:07.326 --> 06:09.744
[gasps] Wait, Akiyama?

06:11.038 --> 06:12.371
What are you doing here?

06:12.413 --> 06:14.749
And how'd you know
where to find me?

06:14.791 --> 06:16.918
Well, I figured you were
in some kind of trouble

06:16.960 --> 06:19.171
after you stopped blowing up
my phone every day.

06:19.213 --> 06:22.423
I asked the LGT Office about it,
and wouldn't you know,

06:22.465 --> 06:24.718
they said you'd entered
the revival round.

06:24.759 --> 06:27.054
And here you are, sobbing away.

06:27.095 --> 06:28.805
Things not going well,
I take it?

06:28.847 --> 06:30.807
[Nao cries]

06:32.351 --> 06:35.729
I messed it all up, Akiyama!
[cries]

06:35.770 --> 06:37.231
Good grief.

06:38.023 --> 06:40.150
[NAO] Eventually,
I pulled myself together

06:40.192 --> 06:41.943
and told him everything.

06:41.985 --> 06:43.737
What do I do?

06:43.778 --> 06:45.947
Even luck seems to hate me now.

06:45.989 --> 06:48.158
It does seem that way.

06:48.616 --> 06:50.451
Good news is,
luck had nothing to do

06:50.493 --> 06:52.162
with why you lost that game.

06:52.204 --> 06:53.372
[NAO] Huh?

06:53.747 --> 06:56.166
The very notion that you had
a fifty-fifty shot at winning

06:56.208 --> 06:58.085
is a giant pile of BS.

06:58.126 --> 07:00.921
No luck, just Fukunaga
pulling strings

07:00.962 --> 07:02.589
to make sure
she got what she wanted.

07:02.630 --> 07:03.715
She what?

07:03.757 --> 07:05.926
How do you know that?

07:05.967 --> 07:09.388
Answer me this first.
Why'd she assign you the Joker?

07:09.428 --> 07:11.223
But she didn't assign it to me.

07:11.265 --> 07:13.432
She asked if I preferred light
or darkness,

07:13.474 --> 07:16.103
and I said light.
That's why I got the Joker card.

07:16.144 --> 07:18.813
So "light" here means
the card's face.

07:18.855 --> 07:22.025
Okay, and what would've changed
if you'd picked "darkness?"

07:22.067 --> 07:24.027
Uh, well, she'd have the Joker.

07:24.069 --> 07:25.653
- No, she wouldn't.
- [gasps]

07:25.695 --> 07:27.281
Your answer never mattered

07:27.322 --> 07:29.241
because the metaphor
was just to distract you

07:29.283 --> 07:31.785
from realizing she was
setting you up to fail.

07:31.826 --> 07:34.079
You were always
getting the Joker,

07:34.121 --> 07:36.455
because the game
is stacked against it.

07:36.497 --> 07:39.084
How? It was just the two cards.

07:39.126 --> 07:40.459
It's not about the cards.

07:40.501 --> 07:42.337
It's about how you played
the game.

07:42.921 --> 07:46.507
Fukunaga mixed the cards,
then you drew one from the bag.

07:47.884 --> 07:49.886
At this point,
the chance that you'd pull

07:49.928 --> 07:52.431
the double-backed card
was 50%.

07:53.056 --> 07:54.891
But when you drew
a card face up,

07:54.933 --> 07:56.935
you put it back in the bag.

07:56.977 --> 07:58.270
[Nao gasps]

07:59.438 --> 08:01.106
See the trick now?

08:01.940 --> 08:04.567
Fukunaga's card
had two backs to it.

08:04.609 --> 08:06.236
It couldn't be drawn face up,

08:06.278 --> 08:08.613
so it would never be returned
to the bag.

08:08.655 --> 08:11.616
But your card had a face
and a back,

08:11.658 --> 08:14.035
so there was
a baked in 50% chance of it

08:14.077 --> 08:15.620
being returned to the bag.

08:15.662 --> 08:16.704
REVERSE+REVERSE = FUKUNAGA WINS

08:16.955 --> 08:18.832
So basically, you were
only getting the Joker

08:18.873 --> 08:20.250
a third of the time.

08:20.292 --> 08:21.500
REVERSE+FACE = NAO WINS
FACE = RESTART

08:21.542 --> 08:22.752
With those odds,

08:22.919 --> 08:26.256
the chances of being the first
to ten points are 6%,

08:26.298 --> 08:28.633
not all that likely to happen.

08:28.675 --> 08:30.593
Honestly, I'm surprised
the game lasted

08:30.635 --> 08:31.970
as long as you said.

08:32.012 --> 08:33.430
[Nao sighs]

08:33.888 --> 08:36.557
Why am I always
such a complete idiot?

08:36.599 --> 08:38.977
Fukunaga would never play
a fair game.

08:39.019 --> 08:40.937
Well, don't just cry about it.

08:40.979 --> 08:43.482
Get back out there
and make her pay.

08:43.522 --> 08:44.941
[NAO] Huh?

08:45.942 --> 08:47.068
[Hitomi grunts softly]

08:47.402 --> 08:49.863
[HITOMI] They could've
at least let us play the games.

08:49.904 --> 08:51.239
[NAO] Hey, Fukunaga.

08:51.281 --> 08:52.573
[HITOMI] Hm?

08:52.615 --> 08:54.242
I want a rematch,

08:54.284 --> 08:57.120
and I won't take no
for an answer, got it?

08:57.620 --> 08:58.746
[HITOMI] What's this?

08:58.997 --> 09:01.041
Don't tell me she figured out
the game's rigged.

09:01.082 --> 09:02.501
I respect the hustle,

09:02.667 --> 09:05.504
but I'm not too keen on rolling
those particular dice again.

09:05.544 --> 09:08.006
[NAO] I understand why
you'd feel that way.

09:08.048 --> 09:10.425
Which is why I'm prepared
to change the terms

09:10.467 --> 09:12.593
to make them
more appealing to you.

09:12.635 --> 09:14.012
So, how does this sound?

09:14.054 --> 09:16.306
I won't ask you
for thirty votes.

09:16.348 --> 09:19.434
Just ten. And you'll get
50 million yen if I lose.

09:19.476 --> 09:20.768
[Hitomi gasps]

09:21.895 --> 09:23.021
[HITOMI] Why ten?

09:23.063 --> 09:24.731
You know that's not
near enough for you

09:24.772 --> 09:26.733
to avoid getting downsized.

09:27.317 --> 09:30.611
[NAO] I know, but I have
to compromise on something,

09:30.653 --> 09:33.281
otherwise you'll never agree
to a rematch.

09:33.865 --> 09:35.367
You're that sure you'll win?

09:35.409 --> 09:38.370
I don't think I'd say
that I'm sure about it.

09:38.912 --> 09:41.873
But the odds of winning
are fifty-fifty, aren't they?

09:41.915 --> 09:44.459
And you won last time,
so maybe it's my turn.

09:44.501 --> 09:47.421
That's a good enough reason
to try again, isn't it?

09:47.462 --> 09:50.798
[HITOMI] Never change,
my beautifully stupid hayseed!

09:52.008 --> 09:54.469
I'll do it,
but only on one condition.

09:54.511 --> 09:55.512
[Nao gasps]

09:55.803 --> 09:58.181
We keep the rules exactly
the same as before.

09:58.223 --> 09:59.598
[NAO] That's fine!

09:59.640 --> 10:01.851
Great! Then let's do this thing.

10:01.893 --> 10:05.105
[Nao laughs] She took the bait.
Now everything was set up

10:05.146 --> 10:07.524
to turn Fukunaga's game
against her.

10:11.445 --> 10:12.695
Oh, no!

10:12.737 --> 10:15.614
[laughs] Well,
would you look at that?

10:15.656 --> 10:17.784
Seems history intends
to repeat itself.

10:17.825 --> 10:18.868
NAO
FUKUNAGA

10:18.910 --> 10:21.704
I hope you don't take it
personally.

10:21.746 --> 10:24.458
Why is it that you're winning
so many in a row?

10:24.499 --> 10:26.960
It should be a more even split,
don't you think?

10:28.336 --> 10:29.712
I don't get it.

10:29.754 --> 10:31.506
Could there be
something wrong?

10:31.548 --> 10:33.967
I promise, everything
is as it should be.

10:34.008 --> 10:36.886
Now, quit stalling
and let's bring this home.

10:39.473 --> 10:41.015
[NAO] This is it!

10:42.725 --> 10:44.144
Yeah!

10:45.353 --> 10:46.771
All right!

10:48.022 --> 10:49.816
Oh, wow!

10:50.317 --> 10:52.193
Another point for me!

10:52.235 --> 10:53.903
NAO
FUKUNAGA

10:53.945 --> 10:55.238
[HITOMI] What the hell?

10:55.280 --> 10:57.449
This can't be happening.

10:57.656 --> 10:58.866
You're cheating.

10:58.908 --> 11:00.285
You have to be.

11:01.620 --> 11:04.080
It's not that strange
with fifty-fifty odds.

11:04.122 --> 11:07.000
Plus, you said it's impossible
to cheat at this game.

11:08.376 --> 11:10.462
Kinda weird for you
to think I was.

11:10.504 --> 11:12.631
Unless you knew of a way
someone could cheat.

11:12.671 --> 11:14.757
No, that's not possible.

11:14.799 --> 11:17.760
Fine! Let's just
get this over with, all right?

11:18.470 --> 11:21.264
She's on a lucky streak,
that's all it is.

11:21.306 --> 11:22.765
The game hasn't changed,

11:22.807 --> 11:25.101
and the odds
are still in my favor.

11:26.478 --> 11:30.565
Her luck can't last forever.
This last draw is mine!

11:34.861 --> 11:37.531
Go on. Flip it.

11:42.369 --> 11:44.412
[Hitomi grunting]

11:46.956 --> 11:49.834
I won! Yay me!

11:50.293 --> 11:52.045
But that's not...

11:52.086 --> 11:53.672
It's wrong!

11:53.712 --> 11:54.797
NAO
FUKUNAGA

11:54.839 --> 11:56.174
[HITOMI] This isn't possible.

11:56.216 --> 11:57.925
You have to have cheated.

11:57.967 --> 11:59.678
It's the only way!

11:59.718 --> 12:00.970
You keep saying that.

12:01.012 --> 12:02.096
But according to you,

12:02.138 --> 12:03.598
we had an equal chance
at winning.

12:03.640 --> 12:04.683
And if that's true,

12:05.058 --> 12:07.435
then it shouldn't be
all that weird if I won, right?

12:07.477 --> 12:08.769
Not to be a nag,

12:08.811 --> 12:11.022
but you should make good
on your M Ticket soon,

12:11.064 --> 12:14.234
only have three minutes,
or you're in breach of contract.

12:14.275 --> 12:15.902
Or I'll have to tell the dealer,

12:15.943 --> 12:19.072
and you'll end up getting hit
with a 100 million yen penalty.

12:19.113 --> 12:20.699
[Hitomi grunts]

12:20.739 --> 12:22.659
[HITOMI] Damn it!

12:23.742 --> 12:25.662
[NAO] It had all come together.

12:25.704 --> 12:28.747
And while I had been
the one to execute the plan,

12:28.789 --> 12:30.291
I didn't make it.

12:31.459 --> 12:33.920
We'll give her a taste
of her own medicine.

12:33.961 --> 12:36.839
First, you'll need to get her
to agree to a rematch.

12:36.881 --> 12:38.091
But why though?

12:38.299 --> 12:41.760
Really? You just said
I only have a 6% chance to win.

12:41.802 --> 12:42.970
Playing fair, yes.

12:43.012 --> 12:45.098
But you're going to cheat.

12:45.139 --> 12:46.600
How exactly?

12:46.641 --> 12:47.601
By taking a cue

12:47.642 --> 12:49.352
from a completely
different game.

12:49.394 --> 12:50.604
You'll mark the cards,

12:50.645 --> 12:52.731
like how cheaters mark tiles
in mahjong.

12:52.771 --> 12:53.940
It's called "ganpai."

12:55.024 --> 12:56.109
That might work

12:56.150 --> 12:58.403
if I wasn't blindly
drawing the cards.

12:58.445 --> 13:00.113
A mark's not gonna help me.

13:00.154 --> 13:02.323
It will if you mark it
by touch.

13:02.365 --> 13:04.534
All you need to do
is put a tiny notch

13:04.576 --> 13:06.661
in the side of the card,
and you're good.

13:06.703 --> 13:08.204
Really?

13:10.415 --> 13:13.209
Hey, you're right!
It's small, but I can feel it!

13:13.251 --> 13:14.919
See? Now then,

13:14.961 --> 13:17.589
the best time to mark the card
is right at the start.

13:17.631 --> 13:19.840
Just be sure to mark
the double-backed card

13:19.882 --> 13:21.217
and not the Joker.

13:21.259 --> 13:23.511
After that, you can grab
whichever card you want

13:23.553 --> 13:24.679
whenever you want.

13:24.721 --> 13:25.722
Okay.

13:26.097 --> 13:28.391
Last thing, don't just pull
the Joker every time.

13:28.433 --> 13:31.227
You need to pull the misprint
more often than not.

13:31.269 --> 13:32.353
NAO
FUKUNAGA

13:32.646 --> 13:34.813
So for every two misprint pulls,
do one Joker pull.

13:34.855 --> 13:37.233
[NAO] All right,
but why does that matter?

13:37.816 --> 13:39.402
[AKIYAMA] Fukunaga knows
the game's odds

13:39.444 --> 13:41.655
are rigged two to one
in her favor.

13:41.696 --> 13:43.740
As long as you keep
the illusion of those odds,

13:43.782 --> 13:46.242
she won't get suspicious
of anything.

13:46.660 --> 13:48.995
Now I get it.
If she assumes she'll win,

13:49.036 --> 13:50.622
then she won't suspect
she's being played

13:50.664 --> 13:52.123
until it's too late.

13:52.165 --> 13:54.751
Which will be
when the score's nine to five.

13:54.793 --> 13:58.171
After that, just pull the Joker
and watch the fireworks.

13:58.212 --> 14:00.131
Nine to six,

14:00.173 --> 14:01.800
nine to seven.

14:01.840 --> 14:05.386
That'll be when Fukunaga might
start to notice something's off.

14:05.428 --> 14:08.682
She'll fixate on the Joker
because that's your card.

14:08.723 --> 14:10.891
But the card that's
actually making her lose

14:10.933 --> 14:12.935
will be tucked away in the bag.

14:12.977 --> 14:14.312
Oh, right!

14:14.354 --> 14:16.189
That's why
I'm marking the misprint.

14:16.230 --> 14:17.940
I was wondering why you said to.

14:17.982 --> 14:20.443
[AKIYAMA] Nine to eight
is the tipping point.

14:20.485 --> 14:22.278
Fukunaga will know
something's up

14:22.320 --> 14:23.988
and will start pointing fingers.

14:24.614 --> 14:27.408
And that's fine.
She can't change anything.

14:27.450 --> 14:29.160
She'll need
more than two draws

14:29.202 --> 14:32.539
to suss out the trick,
but that's all she'll have.

14:34.541 --> 14:37.669
[NAO] And that's how
I got one over on Fukunaga.

14:39.713 --> 14:41.297
[LERONIRA]
Thank you for your patience

14:41.339 --> 14:43.257
while we updated the tallies.

14:43.299 --> 14:44.217
NAO KANZAKI - 0

14:44.258 --> 14:45.385
[LERONIRA] Apologies.

14:45.802 --> 14:48.304
It seems we failed to include
a change in the vote totals.

14:48.346 --> 14:49.347
[all gasp]

14:49.389 --> 14:50.849
What does that mean?

14:50.889 --> 14:51.932
No idea.

14:55.353 --> 14:56.437
YUJI FUKUNAGA - 25
NAO KANZAKI - 10

14:56.479 --> 14:57.480
[all gasp]

14:57.689 --> 14:59.982
Where the hell did Nao
get ten votes from?

15:00.024 --> 15:02.318
Yeah, and why did Fukunaga
suddenly lose votes?

15:02.360 --> 15:03.403
Not cool!

15:03.820 --> 15:06.113
[LERONIRA] The next vote
will take place in one hour.

15:06.155 --> 15:08.199
- Thank you.
- [Hitomi scoffs]

15:08.241 --> 15:09.283
Come back.

15:09.325 --> 15:11.536
We've got questions,
Fukunaga!

15:16.332 --> 15:19.419
[HITOMI] I hope you're happy
with your measly ten votes.

15:19.460 --> 15:22.088
Because that's as close
as you'll get to winning.

15:23.631 --> 15:25.007
[Akiyama chuckles]

15:25.049 --> 15:26.384
Very well done.

15:26.426 --> 15:28.302
I'm sad I wasn't there
to see it.

15:28.344 --> 15:30.012
- [NAO] Akiyama...
- Hm?

15:30.054 --> 15:31.848
Are you sure I can win?

15:31.890 --> 15:33.725
Of course I'm sure.

15:33.767 --> 15:36.227
Those "measly" votes
are just a tool.

15:36.269 --> 15:38.772
So, take them
and carve your path forward.

15:38.979 --> 15:41.775
SEVENTH VOTE

15:42.525 --> 15:45.570
EIGHTH VOTE

15:48.406 --> 15:49.657
[Hitomi chuckles]

15:50.157 --> 15:51.992
Told you, flail all you want,

15:52.034 --> 15:55.037
but your neck's still
on the chopping block. [scoffs]

15:55.580 --> 15:56.664
[NAO] She was right.

15:56.873 --> 15:59.709
I was flailing,
but not because I was scared.

16:00.293 --> 16:01.377
It was an act.

16:01.419 --> 16:03.296
I had to play the victim
for Fukunaga

16:03.337 --> 16:05.256
so she wouldn't see me
as a threat.

16:05.298 --> 16:09.469
And after she'd written me off,
I got to work.

16:12.096 --> 16:13.514
[NAO] Kikuzawa!

16:14.432 --> 16:15.683
Can I talk to you?

16:15.725 --> 16:17.393
I need your help with something.

16:17.435 --> 16:20.187
Huh? Yeah, no.

16:20.229 --> 16:21.397
Whatever it is,

16:21.481 --> 16:23.566
it'll have to wait
until after the game's over.

16:23.608 --> 16:24.734
[NAO] No, wait!

16:24.776 --> 16:26.360
I'll give you 70 million!

16:26.402 --> 16:28.780
- [Kikuzawa gasps]
- But only if you help me.

16:28.822 --> 16:30.824
So please, just hear me out!

16:31.491 --> 16:33.284
I've only gotten ten votes.

16:33.326 --> 16:34.368
And I'm pretty sure

16:34.410 --> 16:36.370
I won't get any more
before the end.

16:36.412 --> 16:39.039
So, I've accepted
that I'm going to lose.

16:39.081 --> 16:41.292
Sucks that
things had to go down this way.

16:41.334 --> 16:44.128
It's fine.
I can't begrudge anyone

16:44.170 --> 16:46.547
when we're all playing
the same game.

16:46.589 --> 16:49.843
But there is one thing
I can't accept.

16:50.468 --> 16:52.553
My loss means Fukunaga stays,

16:52.595 --> 16:54.430
and she earned
a lot of money this game.

16:54.472 --> 16:56.098
That's gonna give her
an unfair advantage

16:56.140 --> 16:57.057
in round three.

16:57.099 --> 16:58.852
What do you mean "earned?"

16:58.893 --> 17:01.019
You know we paid her
not to vote for you?

17:01.061 --> 17:04.190
I do, and like I said,
no hard feelings.

17:04.231 --> 17:07.735
But she stole 30 million from me
on top of what you gave her.

17:07.777 --> 17:09.487
She stole 30 million yen?

17:09.529 --> 17:13.073
But that means she's got
70 million over the rest of us.

17:13.115 --> 17:14.826
That's what I'm saying!

17:14.868 --> 17:16.703
Think about what that means!

17:16.744 --> 17:17.954
With such a massive lead,

17:18.287 --> 17:20.957
she's gonna win round three
just by walking into the room!

17:20.999 --> 17:23.041
Oh, man, this is not good.

17:23.083 --> 17:24.126
I know!

17:24.377 --> 17:26.671
After the way she lied
and manipulated all of you

17:26.713 --> 17:28.255
to win the second game,

17:28.297 --> 17:30.675
she doesn't deserve to win
anything anymore.

17:30.717 --> 17:32.050
Yeah, I agree.

17:32.092 --> 17:33.135
I'm glad.

17:33.344 --> 17:35.805
'Cause I want to give you
what I have left.

17:35.847 --> 17:37.598
Use that money to stop her.

17:37.640 --> 17:38.850
Wait, what?

17:38.892 --> 17:40.560
After I realized
what was happening,

17:40.601 --> 17:43.103
I started observing
how everyone's been playing.

17:43.145 --> 17:44.605
I believe that you're
the best person

17:44.647 --> 17:46.440
to beat Fukunaga
in the third game!

17:46.482 --> 17:48.860
What, for real?
You really think so?

17:48.902 --> 17:50.444
You're an automotive engineer,

17:50.486 --> 17:52.613
so you know systems
and mechanics,

17:52.655 --> 17:55.033
that's a powerful edge
to have in this game.

17:55.073 --> 17:57.827
But what really convinced me
was the courage that you showed

17:57.869 --> 18:00.162
when you stood up
to that LGT official!

18:00.204 --> 18:01.873
[Kikuzawa chuckles]

18:01.915 --> 18:04.542
[NAO] The only thing
Fukunaga has over you is money,

18:04.584 --> 18:06.293
and that's something
I can help you with.

18:06.335 --> 18:07.378
[KIKUZAWA] Hm.

18:07.420 --> 18:08.671
So take it.

18:08.713 --> 18:11.340
I'll give you the 70 million
that I have left.

18:11.382 --> 18:12.675
Then you'll be even.

18:12.717 --> 18:14.385
And since you're
the stronger player,

18:14.427 --> 18:15.553
she won't stand a chance.

18:15.595 --> 18:17.555
- I know you can win!
- Well, yeah.

18:17.597 --> 18:19.599
I'm not disagreeing
with you or anything.

18:19.640 --> 18:23.352
It's just, are you sure?
70 million is a lot of money.

18:23.394 --> 18:26.272
Obviously, I can't just
give it to you for nothing.

18:27.065 --> 18:30.902
And so, I want you to transfer
ten of your votes to me.

18:30.944 --> 18:33.320
Uh... Transfer votes?

18:33.362 --> 18:34.655
That's not... What?

18:34.697 --> 18:36.866
Isn't that like,
against the rules or something?

18:36.908 --> 18:38.034
It's not.

18:38.242 --> 18:40.453
The votes we've earned
are just another resource.

18:40.494 --> 18:42.496
We can do
what we want with them.

18:42.538 --> 18:43.581
I'll prove it.

18:43.706 --> 18:45.666
Remember what happened
in the sixth vote?

18:45.708 --> 18:47.919
I won a bet against Fukunaga
for ten votes,

18:47.961 --> 18:49.837
so the dealer
took it from her total.

18:50.337 --> 18:51.881
So that's what happened.

18:51.923 --> 18:54.258
In that case,
why just another ten?

18:54.300 --> 18:56.677
It's what I need
to be the most help to you.

18:56.719 --> 18:57.887
When I asked about the votes,

18:57.929 --> 18:59.722
the official said that
other revival rounds

18:59.764 --> 19:00.848
were happening.

19:00.890 --> 19:02.600
This is a tournament,
so that tracks.

19:02.642 --> 19:04.685
Yes, and apparently,
someone dropped out.

19:04.727 --> 19:06.479
So now there's
an open slot they need

19:06.520 --> 19:08.731
- to fill for round three.
- Ah!

19:08.773 --> 19:10.775
But they don't have
many options.

19:10.817 --> 19:13.151
So, they're looking
at the downsized players.

19:13.193 --> 19:16.322
They said they'll pick the one
who has secured the most votes.

19:16.363 --> 19:18.074
That means what?

19:18.116 --> 19:20.158
Well, the other games
have already ended,

19:20.200 --> 19:22.160
so I know the number
that I need to beat.

19:22.202 --> 19:23.955
If I can beat nineteen votes,

19:23.997 --> 19:27.541
then I can take the open spot,
and I have ten right now.

19:27.583 --> 19:28.876
And if I give you ten more,

19:28.918 --> 19:30.711
you'll move on
with the rest of us.

19:30.753 --> 19:33.213
Which is why I'm only asking
that much from you.

19:33.798 --> 19:36.216
Everyone knows
I can't avoid getting downsized.

19:36.258 --> 19:37.760
So, it doesn't matter
where you place,

19:37.802 --> 19:40.178
because you're moving
onto round three anyway.

19:40.262 --> 19:41.848
Which means,
over half of the votes

19:41.889 --> 19:44.433
in your total
are completely meaningless.

19:44.475 --> 19:45.726
They're dead weight.

19:45.768 --> 19:47.478
You might as well
make some money for yourself

19:47.520 --> 19:48.562
and sell them.

19:49.105 --> 19:51.357
And if you sell them to me,
I can save my place in the game!

19:51.398 --> 19:53.693
You're right!
It's totally a win-win!

19:53.734 --> 19:56.029
[NAO] It's more
than a win-win, actually.

19:56.070 --> 19:59.073
Because having me stay
gives you an ally,

19:59.115 --> 20:01.868
and I've already proven
that you can trust me.

20:01.909 --> 20:03.494
So, let's do it!

20:04.495 --> 20:05.955
[KIKUZAWA] Huh.

20:06.580 --> 20:09.207
[KIKUZAWA] I can enter
the third game with enough money

20:09.249 --> 20:11.209
to take down Fukunaga,

20:11.251 --> 20:13.337
and I'll have someone there
to back me up?

20:13.379 --> 20:15.339
- [NAO] So what do you say?
- Uh?

20:16.465 --> 20:19.593
You can count on me!
Let's win this thing!

20:19.635 --> 20:21.679
[NAO] Thank you so much!

20:22.555 --> 20:24.015
[NAO]
And so, we had a deal,

20:24.057 --> 20:26.350
with some additions
to the final contract.

20:26.976 --> 20:28.936
He would get
the rest of my 70 million,

20:28.978 --> 20:31.480
but only after the votes
had been transferred to me.

20:31.522 --> 20:32.732
In other words,

20:32.857 --> 20:34.942
he'd only get paid out
after the ninth vote.

20:35.233 --> 20:37.403
But before we entered
into the tenth...

20:37.444 --> 20:38.445
TRANSACTION WITH: NAO KANZAKI

20:38.487 --> 20:39.780
...and while
we didn't exactly

20:39.822 --> 20:41.239
write out a whole NDA,

20:41.323 --> 20:44.202
we did agree to keep quiet
about the nature of our deal.

20:44.242 --> 20:46.120
[KIKUZAWA]
Okay, it all looks good!

20:46.162 --> 20:47.205
Man, I'm pumped!

20:47.245 --> 20:48.873
I can't wait
to get into the next game

20:48.915 --> 20:50.666
and wipe the floor
with Fukunaga!

20:50.708 --> 20:52.168
Yeah!

20:53.794 --> 20:57.215
[NAO] With that done,
the ninth vote came and went.

20:58.591 --> 21:01.677
[LERONIRA] Who's ready to see
the results of our last vote?

21:04.430 --> 21:07.641
[LERONIRA] Who's ready to see
how you moved your votes around?

21:08.142 --> 21:09.769
[KIKUZAWA] Here we go!

21:09.810 --> 21:13.064
Me losing ten and Nao
gaining ten will look weird,

21:13.106 --> 21:15.733
but it's too late
for anyone to do anything.

21:15.775 --> 21:16.817
[beep]

21:17.401 --> 21:19.237
- [all gasp]
- [KIKUZAWA] Huh?

21:19.277 --> 21:21.155
- It's not that weird.
- [Hitomi gasps]

21:21.197 --> 21:22.406
[indistinct chatter]

21:22.448 --> 21:23.407
[Kikuzawa gasps]

21:23.449 --> 21:24.366
NAO KANZAKI - 80

21:24.408 --> 21:25.367
[KIKUZAWA] No.

21:25.409 --> 21:27.453
What the hell did you do?

21:27.494 --> 21:29.496
Nao, what do you think
you're doing?

21:29.538 --> 21:31.582
This wasn't the deal!

21:31.707 --> 21:32.959
No, it is.

21:33.709 --> 21:35.044
There's ten from you,

21:35.086 --> 21:37.088
and ten votes
from everyone else.

21:37.130 --> 21:40.133
But that means
you made deals with all of us?

21:40.174 --> 21:41.341
[all gasping softly]

21:41.383 --> 21:43.970
You tricked me, you hag!

21:44.011 --> 21:46.139
[AKIYAMA] There's no cause
for name-calling.

21:46.180 --> 21:47.347
[Kikuzawa grunts]

21:47.389 --> 21:50.059
It is a game, remember?

21:50.101 --> 21:52.394
And this is how
that game is played.

21:53.311 --> 21:54.438
So shut it.

21:54.480 --> 21:56.232
What? Who let you in here?

21:56.274 --> 21:57.900
How long have you been
standing there?

21:57.942 --> 22:00.236
[AKIYAMA] Why are you all
suddenly obsessed with me?

22:00.278 --> 22:02.738
I'm not the one
who just broke the game.

22:03.447 --> 22:07.409
You've all just handed
Nao Kanzaki absolute power.

22:07.451 --> 22:10.621
And believe me,
she's sure gonna wield it.

22:10.663 --> 22:13.540
I suggest you try
to get on her good side.

22:15.542 --> 22:17.962
[♪ closing theme song playing]

23:44.924 --> 23:49.970
NEXT TIME
SALVATION
